MODULE environment

FUNCTION profile binary paths
    require every locked package to be healthy
    resolve each declared binary directory beneath its package store
    require every result to be a directory
    return paths in profile order without duplicates

FUNCTION print shell activation
    for bash or zsh, fish, PowerShell, or cmd, safely quote all paths for that
        shell and prepend them to its path variable
    reject unsupported shells and shell-specific unsafe path characters

FUNCTION open profile shell
    derive verified binary paths
    prepend them to the child environment only
    choose the current user shell, cmd.exe on Windows, or /bin/sh on Unix when
        the configured shell is missing or invalid
    start it interactively with inherited input and output
    return when the child shell exits without editing startup files
